# Sign in with your Python client

Install Python 3.11 or newer and Chrome or Chromium. From this directory, install
the generated package and its dependencies in your Python environment.

```sh
python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt
```

If you generated this client with a website login URL, run `python3 client.py login`.
To choose the starting page yourself, enter the website's HTTPS login address when prompted
by these shell commands.

```sh
printf 'Website login URL: '
read -r login_url
python3 client.py login --url "$login_url"
```

Complete sign-in and MFA in the browser. Once you see the intended dashboard,
return to the terminal and press Enter. The command closes its browser and prints
`{"authentication": "user-confirmed", "sessionClosed": true}`. Use
`--browser chromium` for Chromium or `--browser-path` for a specific executable.
Cancel with Ctrl+C and run the same command again to retry.

Each login starts a fresh browser. The generated directory contains no passwords
or cookies.
